sara_cs: Hey team — Helios (trial) is seeing a burst of 429s right after SDK init during warmup. Reported ~200 parallel preflight calls on first user session. Link: https://helios.app/dashboard

matt_eng: Can you paste the SDK init snippet and any response headers from the 429s?

sara_cs: Here’s what they send on init (redacted):
```
POST /v1/sessions/init
Authorization: Bearer sk_live_***
X-Client: helios-web/1.2.0
body: { sessions: [..], creds: { ephemeral: true }}
```
And example 429 response headers: `x-rate-limit: 100; x-retry-after: 2`

carmen_support: hmm looks like token fanout + no client-side throttling. Are they creating a fresh ephemeral token per tab? :thinking_face:

leo_infra: I pulled the gateway logs for their key — spikes exactly at 08:12:02 UTC with 180 concurrent handshake requests. Backend rate window is per-api-key with short burst tolerance. This is classic warmup stampede.

matt_eng: Suggested quick mitigations:
- clamp concurrent init requests client-side to 8-10
- add exponential backoff with jitter on 429 (randomized 250-750ms base)
- cache ephemeral token per session (avoid per-request new token)

sara_cs: I pinged Helios and they said they spin up 10 iframes for previews (ouch). I'll ask them to throttle to 6 while we validate.

leo_infra: Also we can add a temporary soft quota bump for their trial org for next 24h to avoid churn. Ops: would you like me to open a quick support quota?

matt_eng: Yes please, + add a short-lived override in the rate limiter for org_id=org_helios with burst=400 for 6h. I'll watch error rates.

deploy-bot: deploy 2026-03-20T08:10:00Z by matt_eng — rate-limiter hotfix queued (id: dpl-8821).

carmen_support: One more long-term note for onboarding playbook: include SDK warmup best-practices (cache ephemeral tokens, limit concurrent preflights, show snippet for jittered retries). I'll add to enablement checklist.

sara_cs: Thanks everyone — Helios will try client-side clamp now. Will report back in 30m. I’ll also share the recommended code snippet. :thumbsup:

matt_eng: Example client retry (JS):
```
async function sendWithBackoff(fn){
  let attempt=0;
  while(true){
    try{ return await fn(); }catch(e){
      if(e.status!==429 || attempt>6) throw e;
      const wait = Math.floor(Math.random() * (500 * Math.pow(2, attempt))) + 100;
      await new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r, wait));
      attempt++;
    }
  }
}
```

sara_cs: Update: they reduced concurrency to 5 and 429s dropped to single-digit/min. Keeping temporary quota bump for 4h. I'll close after monitoring.

leo_infra: Logs look green. Please file a short note in the onboarding playbook with the Helios example so CSMs can pre-check for iframe spawns.

sara_cs: Will do. Closing in 2h if stable. :white_check_mark:
